# A VARIANT, NEVER THE PRODUCT: ON TOP OF v-hide-by-vector, THE TYRE'S FOOT WHERE THAT CUT STILL MISSES IT, AND ITS TEST MADE CHEAPER AND
# NARROWER (2026-10-27; round 9's tyre desk, docs\reports\fg-5\desk-2026-10-27-tyres: FINDINGS.md). IT CHANGES THE PICTURE, ONLY WHERE
# THE OCCLUSION TEST CALLED THE FRAME BEFORE'S SAMPLE VISIBLE.
#
# WHAT IS LEFT AFTER v-hide-by-vector, on the capture of 2026-10-27:
#   THE BOUNCE. The tyre bounces on its springs: between two real frames its foot moves up by a few pixels (4.2 px in run 5; its
#     vector says so). The road just under the new foot is tyre in the frame before and road now, so neither AMD's depth test (the
#     contact: within half a percent) nor v-hide-by-vector's (the vector at the place is the road's now) sees it.
#   THE CONTACT ROW. At the very foot the road the pixel shows lies lower on the screen than the tyre's last row at the fetch place,
#     a little NEARER than it, and AMD's test weighs only a tap that is nearer than the pixel: it never weighs that tap.
#   Both leave a thin dark band, a copy of the foot's edge, half a road step behind it.
# AND v-hide-by-vector TOOK A THING THAT MOVES FASTER THAN THE PIXEL TOO (a lamp post before a far wall while the camera pans: it made
# more of the product's doubled post, run 3 frame 10), and it read the vector at each of the four taps of the test: 11.8 us a
# generated frame on the game's frames (tools\test-fg-own\fgtime.cpp, run 5), not the 1 us of the made picture.
# THE CUT, in the occlusion pass, for the frame before's side alone, ONCE A PIXEL that moves (whole vector over HBV_MIN_PX):
#   the current frame's dilated vector AT THE FETCH PLACE: the thing there STAYS where it moves unlike the pixel (v-hide-by-vector's
#     rule) and at most HBV_STAY (a quarter) of the pixel's motion: the car and its tyres over the streaming road. That one answer
#     stands for the four taps (v-hide-by-vector's per-tap read is replaced by it); and a tap a little FARTHER than the pixel (by
#     less than HBV_BEHIND, the contact row) is weighed too where the thing stays;
#   the current frame's dilated vector REACH px ABOVE the fetch place: where the thing there stays and ITS OWN VECTOR TAKES IT ONTO THE
#     FETCH PLACE in the frame before (within REACH_TOL px), and it is not farther than the pixel by more than REACH_DEPTH, it stood
#     there: the frame before's sample is hidden (the bounce).
# Two vector reads and one depth read a moving pixel, issued together.
what A VARIANT (the picture changes): on top of v-hide-by-vector, its test made once a pixel and only for a thing that stays (a quarter of the pixel's motion at most), weighed also at a tap a little farther than the pixel (the tyre's contact row), and a thing that stays found a few pixels above the fetch place whose own vector puts it there in the frame before (the tyre that bounced)
passes ffx_frameinterpolation_disocclusion_mask_pass
wave64 the same edits in both variants: no wave operation; not run here on a wave64 device
file framegeneration/fsr3/include/gpu/frameinterpolation/ffx_frameinterpolation_disocclusion_mask.h
--- old
FFX_STATIC const FfxFloat32 HBV_MIN_PX = 8.0f;
--- new
FFX_STATIC const FfxFloat32 HBV_MIN_PX = 8.0f;
// (the variant v-hide-reach)
FFX_STATIC const FfxFloat32 HBV_STAY    = 0.25f;   // the thing at the fetch place moves at most this share of the pixel's motion
FFX_STATIC const FfxFloat32 HBV_BEHIND  = 0.02f;   // a tap farther than the pixel by less than this share is weighed too (the contact row: 1 to 1.5 percent)
FFX_STATIC const FfxFloat32 REACH       = 4.0f;    // render pixels above the fetch place
FFX_STATIC const FfxFloat32 REACH_TOL   = 3.0f;    // render pixels
FFX_STATIC const FfxFloat32 REACH_DEPTH = 0.02f;   // the thing may lie this share farther than the pixel
static FfxBoolean g_hbvStays = false;                // the thing at the fetch place stays (set once a pixel, before the test)

// does the thing with this vector (render px) stay while the pixel (g_hbvWhole) streams?
FfxBoolean hbvStaying(FfxFloat32x2 fTherePx)
{
    const FfxFloat32x2 fHerePx = g_hbvWhole * FfxFloat32x2(RenderSize());
    const FfxFloat32x2 fDiffPx = fHerePx - fTherePx;
    const FfxFloat32   fHere2  = dot(fHerePx, fHerePx);
    return dot(fDiffPx, fDiffPx) > ffxMax(HBV_MIN_PX * HBV_MIN_PX, HBV_SHARE * HBV_SHARE * fHere2) && dot(fTherePx, fTherePx) < HBV_STAY * HBV_STAY * fHere2;
}
--- end
file framegeneration/fsr3/include/gpu/frameinterpolation/ffx_frameinterpolation_disocclusion_mask.h
--- old
